description:
resolveImport in packages/moe-daemon/src/delivery/architectureRules.ts (lines 476-480) tries joined+ext before joined/index for '.', '..', a trailing '/' or a trailing '/.'. Node and TS resolve those forms to the directory only.

That lets a decoy sibling file bypass a forbid. Repro, probe on HEAD 7f04b869:
- tree {src/state.ts, src/state/index.ts}; one rule, from src/ui, forbid src/state;
- src/ui/v.ts contains `import x from '../state/'`;
- it resolves to src/state.ts, and evaluateArchitecture returns passed. Without the decoy it returns failed.

Fix: index-only candidates for those forms, plus V1 tests. This was QA's round-1 advisory on CQ-V10a (task-2cd62d2c). It is deferred because that task's bytes are frozen under size waiver prop-7401cd0b.
